@startuml STM-10
!include _style.iuml
title STM-10 (System level) — Lifecycle of a Refund\nrefunds.status · v1.1 · 10/11/2026

[*] --> requested : / send refund to\noriginal source
note left of requested
  created by the Admin (kind top_up,
  late_payment) or by the system when a
  Driver closes the account (account_closure);
  one per top-up for top_up and late_payment,
  closure refunds can be several per top-up
end note
requested : attempt fails [transient and attempts < 4]\n/ record error
requested : after(retry delay) [last attempt failed]\n/ query gateway, send again if not received
requested --> done : gateway confirms\n/ request adjustment invoice\n(STM-7), notify Driver
requested --> failed : attempt fails [rejected\nor attempts ≥ 4]\n/ list on Billing Exceptions,\nnotify Admin
failed --> requested : Admin retries\n/ one attempt,\ncounter not reset
done --> [*]
note right of failed
  A failed refund is only retried,
  never put back on the balance.
  Retry delays: 5 min, 30 min, 2 h.
end note
@enduml
